<main id="main-content">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-atmosphere" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="wash wash-mint"></span>
      <span class="wash wash-sand"></span>
      <span class="measure-line line-one"></span>
      <span class="measure-line line-two"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="shell hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Trading infrastructure for agents</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">The trading platform <em>for your agents.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-summary">Give your agents a policy-aware way to analyze connected portfolios, propose strategies, and prepare multi-chain trades. You define the mandate, keep custody, and control authorization.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-dark" href="https://app.runsherpa.ai">Launch Sherpa <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button button-quiet" href="#control">See the control model <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">Your keys and authorization stay with you.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="loop-stage" aria-label="Sherpa routes agent trading through policy checks and wallet authorization">
        <div class="stage-label label-top">agent mandate</div>
        <div class="stage-label label-bottom">authorization</div>
        <div class="loop-orbit orbit-outer" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="loop-orbit orbit-inner" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <span class="orbit-arrow arrow-one" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span class="orbit-arrow arrow-two" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <article class="loop-card loop-card-agent">
          <span class="card-index">01</span>
          <span class="card-kicker">Context</span>
          <strong>Agent</strong>
          <span class="card-detail">portfolio + intent</span>
        </article>
        <article class="loop-card loop-card-policy">
          <span class="card-index">02</span>
          <span class="card-kicker">Guardrail</span>
          <strong>Policy</strong>
          <span class="card-detail">scope + limits</span>
        </article>
        <article class="loop-card loop-card-wallet">
          <span class="card-index">03</span>
          <span class="card-kicker">Control</span>
          <strong>Your wallet</strong>
          <span class="card-detail">review + sign</span>
        </article>
        <div class="loop-core" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="core-pulse"></span>
          <span>S</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles" aria-label="Sherpa operating principles">
    <div class="shell principles-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="principle-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Agent context</h2>
          <p>Useful portfolio and mandate context before an agent suggests a move.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="principle-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Non-custodial</h2>
          <p>Connected wallets stay in your control. Sherpa does not take custody.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="principle-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Policy layer</h2>
          <p>Clear limits help shape what an agent can prepare for your review.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section context-section" id="context" aria-labelledby="context-title">
    <div class="shell split-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">01 / Agent context</p>
        <h2 id="context-title">Give every trading agent the right context.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section-lede">
        <p>Sherpa turns connected portfolio information and your trading instructions into a working brief your agents can use.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="#control">See how the controls work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shell question-grid">
      <p class="question-intro">Ask with context, not from a blank slate.</p>
      <ol class="question-list">
        <li><span>01</span><p>“What changed across my connected wallets this week?”</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><p>“Does this trade fit the mandate I set for this agent?”</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><p>“Prepare the next recurring buy within my approved limits.”</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section strategy-section" id="strategies" aria-labelledby="strategies-title">
    <div class="shell split-heading split-heading-tight">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">02 / Agent strategies</p>
        <h2 id="strategies-title">Give agents a mandate, not a blank check.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-lede">Set the strategy, allowed assets, sizing, cadence, and approval path. Sherpa keeps those instructions attached to the workflow.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell strategy-grid">
      <article class="strategy-card strategy-card-mint">
        <div class="strategy-topline"><span>DCA</span><span>Recurring buys</span></div>
        <h3>Build a disciplined schedule.</h3>
        <p>Instruct an agent to prepare recurring purchases under the cadence, assets, and limits you choose.</p>
        <div class="strategy-rule" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <p class="card-foot">Cadence remains a policy, not a promise.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="strategy-card strategy-card-sand">
        <div class="strategy-topline"><span>COPY</span><span>Strategy following</span></div>
        <h3>Follow a strategy on your terms.</h3>
        <p>Use agent-assisted copy-trading workflows with asset, size, and authorization controls defined up front.</p>
        <div class="copy-steps" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <p class="card-foot">You decide what remains eligible to execute.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="shell mandate-rail" aria-label="Agent strategy workflow">
      <span>Mandate</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Policy</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Review</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Eligible trade</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section execution-section" id="execution" aria-labelledby="execution-title">
    <div class="shell execution-top">
      <p class="section-kicker">03 / Execution layer</p>
      <h2 id="execution-title">Multi-chain trading for agents. Authorization stays with you.</h2>
      <p>Let agents prepare actions across your connected ecosystem, then apply policy checks and choose when to authorize.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell execution-path" aria-label="A transaction moves from agent intent through policy to wallet authorization">
      <article><span class="path-number">01</span><h3>Agent intent</h3><p>An agent reasons from its assigned mandate and portfolio context.</p></article>
      <span class="path-connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <article><span class="path-number">02</span><h3>Policy check</h3><p>Rules shape the assets, scope, and conditions that are permitted.</p></article>
      <span class="path-connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <article><span class="path-number">03</span><h3>Your authorization</h3><p>You retain the final say for actions that require your approval.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section control-section" id="control" aria-labelledby="control-title">
    <div class="shell control-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">04 / Control model</p>
      <h2 id="control-title">A clear path from mandate to controlled trade.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="shell control-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Connect context</h3><p>Bring the relevant wallets and portfolio information into view.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Brief your agents</h3><p>Give each agent the context and responsibility it needs to be useful.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Set the mandate</h3><p>Define the strategy, policy limits, and the approval model that applies.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Review and authorize</h3><p>Inspect prepared actions and retain control of your wallet and approvals.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
    <div class="closing-shape shape-one" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="closing-shape shape-two" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="shell closing-inner">
      <p class="closing-kicker">Your agents. Your policy. Your keys.</p>
      <h2 id="closing-title">Put agents to work without handing over control.</h2>
      <p>Build a more deliberate trading workflow around the agents you trust and the guardrails you define.</p>
      <div class="closing-actions">
        <a class="button button-light" href="https://app.runsherpa.ai">Launch Sherpa <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button button-dark-outline" href="mailto:team@runsherpa.ai">Talk to the team <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

